From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:07:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 003/342] efi/arm64: drop to EL1 before programming the EL1 MMU
 registers

When entered at EL2 without VHE, arm64_common_cpu_startup() set up
TCR/MAIR/TTBR0/TTBR1_EL1 and then called _arch_transition_EL2_EL1, which
copies TTBR0, MAIR and VBAR from EL2 over them. Only the boot CPU has
usable values there (left by the firmware); secondary CPUs started at EL2
by PSCI have reset values, took a translation fault as soon as the MMU was
enabled and spun at VBAR 0 + 0x200, while CPU 0 waited for them forever in
the first boot rendezvous, before any kernel output.

Drop to EL1 first and then do the same MMU setup as the EL1 path. Seen on
the ODROID-C2 (U-Boot runs at EL2) and reproduced with QEMU virt,
virtualization=on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_start.cpp  | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_start.cpp b/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_start.cpp
index f34e07ca15..c832b6a96c 100644
--- a/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_start.cpp
+++ b/src/system/boot/platform/efi/arch/arm64/arch_start.cpp
@@ -64,14 +64,16 @@ arm64_common_cpu_startup()
 
 	// EL2 with E2H enabled behaves as a superset of EL1
 	//
-	// EL2 without E2H enabled does not, so we need to drop to EL1
-	if (el == 1 || e2h) {
-		arm64_mmu_setup();
-		WRITE_SPECIALREG(CNTKCTL_EL1, 0b11);
-	} else {
-		arm64_mmu_setup();
+	// EL2 without E2H enabled does not, so we need to drop to EL1. Do that
+	// before setting up the EL1 MMU registers: the transition copies TTBR0,
+	// MAIR and VBAR from EL2, which only hold usable values on the boot CPU
+	// (left by the firmware). Secondary CPUs started at EL2 by PSCI have reset
+	// values there and would fault as soon as the MMU is enabled.
+	if (el == 2 && !e2h)
 		_arch_transition_EL2_EL1();
-	}
+
+	arm64_mmu_setup();
+	WRITE_SPECIALREG(CNTKCTL_EL1, 0b11);
 
 	WRITE_SPECIALREG(SCTLR_EL1, SCTLR_LSMAOE | SCTLR_nTLSMD
 		| SCTLR_UCI | SCTLR_SPAN | SCTLR_IESB | SCTLR_nTWE | SCTLR_nTWI
